%description:

Tcp.initialSendSequenceNumber:random -- a distribution gives each connection its own ISS.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "volatile, so a distribution gives each connection its own value".

The classes: clock (-1, the default), fixed (a value from 0 to 4294967295), random (a
distribution, which the parameter takes again for each connection, because it is volatile),
invalid (below -1 or above 4294967295). The code: TcpConnection::selectInitialSeqNum(). This test separates "random" from "clock" and "fixed": with them,
two connections that open at the same time have the same ISS.

Host under test: host1, which opens two connections at 0.1 s. Observation: level 1, the two
SYNs of host1 have different sequence numbers.

%# parameter: Tcp.initialSendSequenceNumber
%# class: random
%# value: intuniform(0, 1000000000)
%# key: *.host1.tcp.initialSendSequenceNumber
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpInitialSendSequenceNumberRandom")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .capture("first", "tcp.sequenceNo")
                  .describe("the first SYN of host1")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.sequenceNo != {first}")
                  .describe("the second SYN of host1, with another ISS")
                  .within(0.001));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpInitialSendSequenceNumberRandom compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.initialSendSequenceNumber = intuniform(0, 1000000000)    # the parameter under test
*.host1.numApps = 2
*.host1.app[1].typename = "TcpSessionApp"
*.host1.app[1].connectAddress = "host2"
*.host1.app[1].connectPort = 1000
*.host1.app[1].tSend = 0.2s
*.host1.app[1].sendBytes = 100B
*.host1.app[1].tClose = 1000s
*.host1.app[1].tOpen = 0.1s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpInitialSendSequenceNumberRandom: PASS
